@ifnottex
@node Top
@top ETL Madness Flow

This manual documents the @strong{ETL Madness Flow} command-line utilities
(@command{flow}, @command{crypto_tool}, and @command{db_importer}) and the
@code{<pipeline>} XML workflow specification.

@menu
* Architecture and Standards::  Ecosystem overview, secret precedence, URIs, and exit codes.
* Invoking flow::               Core pipeline engine, validator, builder UI, and repository CLI.
* Invoking crypto_tool::        Encryption, digital signatures, and keypair generation.
* Invoking db_importer::        SQL Server XML repository import and export utility.
* Enterprise Recipes::          End-to-end encrypt-then-sign and options profile workflows.
* Pipeline XML Reference::      Complete @code{<pipeline>} XML elements and attributes.
@end menu
@end ifnottex

@c ==========================================================================
@node Architecture and Standards
@chapter Architecture and Shared Standards

The ETL Madness Flow ecosystem consists of three command-line utilities:

@enumerate
@item
@command{flow}: Primary pipeline execution engine, preflight validator,
XML/AST schema verifier, HTMX visual builder web server, XSLT/Mermaid
transformer, and database import/export manager.
@item
@command{crypto_tool}: Standalone cryptographic utility for AES-256-GCM
encryption/decryption, digital signature signing/verification (OpenSSL,
OpenPGP, PKCS#7/CMS), and asymmetric keypair generation.
@item
@command{db_importer}: Dedicated CLI utility to import and export XML
pipelines, options profiles, and configs in SQL Server repositories
(@code{dbo.flow_*_content}) with UTF-8/UTF-16 auto-detection and at-rest
encryption.
@end enumerate

@section Shared Secret Resolution Precedence

When encryption or decryption operations are performed, passphrases and
cryptographic keys are resolved in the following precedence order:

@enumerate
@item
@strong{Key File} (@option{-key-file @var{path}}) --- Safest: reads the key
directly from a permission-restricted file.
@item
@strong{Command-Line Flag} (@option{-secure-key} or @option{-key}) --- Emits
a warning to @file{stderr} because command-line flags are visible in process
tables (e.g., @command{ps aux}).
@item
@strong{XML Options Profile} (@code{<secure-key>} via @option{-options}) ---
Supported by @command{flow}.
@item
@strong{@env{FLOW_SECURE_KEY}} --- Primary environment variable.
@item
@strong{@env{SECURE_KEY}} --- Fallback environment variable.
@end enumerate

@section Supported Resource URIs

Arguments in @command{flow} that load resources (@option{-file},
@option{-options}, @option{-config}, @option{-import-file}) support uniform
URI resolution:

@table @asis
@item Local File
Standard relative or absolute path, e.g., @file{./pipelines/finance.xml}.
@item HTTP / HTTPS
@code{http://...} or @code{https://...}
@item HTTP Basic Auth
@code{https://Basic%20<base64>@@host/path/etl.xml}
@item SQL Server Query
@code{sql://sqlserver@@<dsn>#<SELECT_QUERY>}
@item Generic DB Alias
@code{db://<driver>@@<dsn>#<SELECT_QUERY>}
@end table

@section Common Exit Codes

All three utilities exit with @code{0} on success and @code{1} on failure
(execution error, validation error, signature verification failure, missing
or invalid decryption key, or database connection error).

@c ==========================================================================
@node Invoking flow
@chapter Invoking @command{flow}

Synopsis:

@example
flow [options...]
@end example

@section @command{flow} Command-Line Options

@table @option
@item -file @var{path|uri}
Path or URI to the XML file containing scripts, databases, and workflow nodes.
Default: @file{scripts.xml}.

@item -options @var{path|uri}
Path or URI to an XML CLI options defaults file
(@code{<flow_cli_options><options>...}). Explicit CLI flags override values
defined in @option{-options}.

@item -config @var{path|uri}
Optional path or URI to a @file{CONFIG.xml} file containing variable and
database connection overrides merged with the base pipeline file.

@item -format @var{format}
Output format for execution results: @code{csv} (default), @code{text},
@code{json}, @code{jsonpretty} (@code{prettyjson}), @code{markdown}
(@code{md}, @code{table}), or @code{stream}.

@item -vars @var{key=value[,...]}
Comma-separated runtime variable overrides. Recursively expands @code{@{@{var@}@}}
placeholders up to 3 levels deep.

@item -validate
Validate XML schema (XSD if @option{-xsd} is set) and AST semantic structure
without executing pipeline nodes.

@item -preflight
Execute only @code{<preflight>} validation nodes, skipping @code{<flow>}.

@item -xsd @var{path}
Path to an @file{.xsd} schema file validated via @command{xmllint} prior to
parsing.

@item -node-output
When logging to a database (@code{log_db}), persist redacted @code{ResultsString}
values to @code{pipeline_events.node_output} on @code{node.finished} rows.
Default: @code{false}.

@item -debug
Enable verbose console logging (connection resolution, dialect detection,
signature metadata, and sink telemetry).

@item -gopath @var{dir}
GOPATH directory for dynamic package imports in the Yaegi Go interpreter.
Defaults to @env{GOPATH}.

@item -xslt @var{path}
Transform pipeline XML using a custom XSLT stylesheet with an auto-generated
Mermaid workflow diagram, then exit.

@item -out @var{path}
Output file path for XSLT-transformed XML produced by @option{-xslt}.

@item -encrypted
Decrypt AES-256-GCM encrypted inputs prior to parsing, or encrypt items
written by @option{-export-file} / @option{-import-file}.

@item -secure-key @var{key}
Symmetric encryption/decryption passphrase or key (warns on @file{stderr}).

@item -key-file @var{path}
Path to file containing the symmetric key/passphrase.

@item -verify-signature
Enforce digital signature verification before decrypting or executing.

@item -public-key @var{path}
PEM public key file (RSA, ECDSA, Ed25519) for signature verification.

@item -cert @var{path}
X.509 certificate file (PEM or DER) for PKCS#7/CMS or X.509 verification.

@item -ca-cert @var{path}
Root or intermediate CA certificate file for chain validation.

@item -keyring @var{path}
OpenPGP armored public keyring file for GPG verification.

@item -signature @var{path}
Detached digital signature file (@file{.sig}, @file{.asc}, @file{.p7s}).
Companion files with matching basenames are checked automatically when omitted.

@item -builder
Start the local HTMX visual pipeline builder web server.

@item -builder-port @var{port}
TCP port for the builder web server (default @code{0} selects an ephemeral
port; falls back to @env{FLOW_BUILDER_PORT} or @env{PORT}).

@item -builder-db @var{path}
SQLite database path for visual builder local storage. Default:
@file{flow_builder.db}.

@item -purge-db
Purge all data from the SQLite visual builder database, re-initialize
defaults, and exit.

@item -import-file @var{path|uri}
Import a pipeline, options, or config XML file into the SQLite builder DB
or external DB (@option{-dsn}).

@item -import-name @var{name}
Custom record name for @option{-import-file} (defaults to file basename).

@item -import-type @var{type}
Item type for @option{-import-file}: @code{pipeline} (default),
@code{options}, or @code{config}.

@item -export-file @var{path}
Destination path to export a record (or @code{-} for @file{stdout}). Disk
files are written with @code{0600} permissions.

@item -export-name @var{name}
Name of the record to export (required with @option{-export-file}).

@item -export-type @var{type}
Item type for @option{-export-file}: @code{pipeline} (default),
@code{options}, or @code{config}.

@item -dsn @var{dsn}
External database DSN for repository import/export (@code{sqlserver},
@code{postgres}, @code{mysql}, @code{sqlite}).
@end table

@section @command{flow} Environment Variables

@itemize @bullet
@item @env{FLOW_SECURE_KEY}, @env{SECURE_KEY}: Symmetric encryption/decryption passphrase.
@item @env{FLOW_BUILDER_PORT}, @env{PORT}: Default port for @option{-builder}.
@item @env{GOPATH}: Go workspace directory for Yaegi package imports.
@item @env{USER} / @env{USERNAME}, @env{HOSTNAME} / @env{COMPUTERNAME}: Recorded in @code{pipeline_runs} audit logs.
@end itemize

@c ==========================================================================
@node Invoking crypto_tool
@chapter Invoking @command{crypto_tool}

Synopsis:

@example
crypto_tool [options...]
@end example

@command{crypto_tool} performs AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption, digital
signing, signature verification, and asymmetric keypair generation.

@section @command{crypto_tool} Command-Line Options

@table @option
@item -action @var{op}
Operation: @code{encrypt} (default), @code{decrypt}, @code{gen-key},
@code{sign}, @code{verify}, or @code{gen-keypair}.

@item -gen-key
Shortcut for @option{-action gen-key}; generates a 256-bit symmetric key.

@item -in @var{path}
Input file path (use @code{-} or omit for @file{stdin}).

@item -out @var{path}
Output file path (use @code{-} or omit for @file{stdout}; secret outputs use
mode @code{0600}).

@item -secure-key @var{key}, -key @var{key}
Passphrase or raw symmetric key (warns on @file{stderr}; falls back to
@env{FLOW_SECURE_KEY} or @env{SECURE_KEY}).

@item -key-file @var{path}
Path to file containing the symmetric key/passphrase.

@item -binary
Emit raw binary ciphertext or ASN.1 signature bytes instead of text-armored
@code{FLOWENC:v1:...} or @code{FLOWSIG:v1:...} envelopes.

@item -sig-type @var{format}
Signature format for @option{-action sign}: @code{openssl} (default; RSA,
ECDSA, Ed25519), @code{pgp} (OpenPGP), or @code{pkcs7} (CMS / PKCS#7).

@item -private-key @var{path}, -priv @var{path}
Private key file path (PEM or OpenPGP) for signing.

@item -passphrase @var{str}
Passphrase to decrypt password-protected private keys.

@item -cert @var{path}
X.509 certificate path (PEM or DER). Required for @option{-sig-type pkcs7}
and supported for verification.

@item -wrap
Bundle signature and payload into a unified @code{FLOWSIGNED:v1:...} envelope.

@item -signature @var{path}, -sig @var{path}
Detached signature path for @option{-action verify} (auto-checks
@file{<in>.sig}, @file{<in>.asc}, @file{<in>.p7s} when omitted).

@item -public-key @var{path}, -pub @var{path}
Public key path (PEM or OpenPGP) for verification.

@item -ca-cert @var{path}
Root or intermediate CA certificate path for chain verification.

@item -keyring @var{path}
OpenPGP armored public keyring path.

@item -keypair-type @var{type}
Algorithm for @option{-action gen-keypair}: @code{rsa} (default),
@code{ecdsa} (P-256), @code{ed25519}, or @code{pgp} (@code{gpg},
@code{openpgp}).

@item -bits @var{n}
RSA modulus bit length (default @code{2048}).

@item -out-priv @var{path}
Output path for generated private key (mode @code{0600}; default
@file{private_key.pem}).

@item -out-pub @var{path}
Output path for generated public key (mode @code{0644}; default
@file{public_key.pem}).

@item -out-cert @var{path}
Optional output path for a 365-day self-signed X.509 certificate.

@item -cn @var{name}
Common Name (@code{CN}) or OpenPGP identity (default @code{Flow Code Signer}).
@end table

@c ==========================================================================
@node Invoking db_importer
@chapter Invoking @command{db_importer}

Synopsis:

@example
db_importer [options...]
@end example

@command{db_importer} imports and exports XML pipelines, CLI options profiles,
and variable configurations in Microsoft SQL Server (@code{dbo.flow_*_content})
using atomic @code{MERGE INTO} upserts and automatic UTF-8 / UTF-16LE /
UTF-16BE BOM translation.

@section @command{db_importer} Command-Line Options

@table @option
@item -action @var{op}
Database operation: @code{import} (default) or @code{export}.

@item -export
Shortcut boolean flag for @option{-action export}.

@item -dsn @var{conn_string}
SQL Server connection string (URL or ADO/ODBC format).

@item -file @var{path}
Input XML path (import) or output path (export). Use @code{-} or empty string
for @file{stdin} / @file{stdout}. Disk exports use @code{0600} permissions.

@item -name @var{key}
Logical record identifier (@code{Name} column) in the target table.

@item -table @var{target}
Target table mapping:
@itemize @bullet
@item @code{pipeline} (default) @result{} @code{dbo.flow_pipeline_content} (@code{PipelineXML})
@item @code{options} @result{} @code{dbo.flow_options_content} (@code{OptionsXML})
@item @code{config} @result{} @code{dbo.flow_config_content} (@code{ConfigXML})
@end itemize

@item -desc @var{text}
Description stored in the @code{Description} column during import.

@item -encrypted
Encrypt XML into @code{FLOWENC:v1:...} before import, or decrypt on export.

@item -secure-key @var{key}
Symmetric passphrase/key (warns on @file{stderr}; falls back to
@env{FLOW_SECURE_KEY} or @env{SECURE_KEY}).

@item -key-file @var{path}
Protected file containing the symmetric passphrase/key.
@end table

@c ==========================================================================
@node Enterprise Recipes
@chapter End-to-End Enterprise Recipes

@section Production CI/CD Release (Encrypt-then-Sign)

@example
# 1. Encrypt the pipeline XML
crypto_tool -action encrypt -in pipeline.xml -out pipeline.xml.enc -key-file prod.key

# 2. Sign the encrypted package into a unified FLOWSIGNED envelope
crypto_tool -action sign -in pipeline.xml.enc -out pipeline.xml.signed \
  -private-key release_priv.pem -wrap

# 3. Import into SQL Server repository
db_importer -dsn "sqlserver://sa:Password@@db:1433?database=ETL" \
  -table pipeline -name "NIGHTLY_SYNC" -file pipeline.xml.signed

# 4. Execute on production host (verifies signature before decrypting)
flow \
  -file "sql://sqlserver@@db:1433?database=ETL#SELECT PipelineXML FROM dbo.flow_pipeline_content WHERE Name='NIGHTLY_SYNC'" \
  -public-key /etc/flow/release_pub.pem \
  -key-file /etc/flow/prod.key
@end example

@section Options Profile Overrides (@option{-options})

@example
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<flow_cli_options>
    <options>
        <format>markdown</format>
        <debug>true</debug>
        <verify-signature>true</verify-signature>
        <public-key>/etc/flow/keys/release_pub.pem</public-key>
        <encrypted>true</encrypted>
    </options>
</flow_cli_options>
@end example

Run @command{flow} with the profile (any explicit CLI flag overrides the XML
profile):

@example
flow -options /etc/flow/prod_options.xml -file /srv/flow/job.xml -key-file /etc/flow/master.key
@end example

