@node Pipeline XML Reference
@chapter @code{<pipeline>} XML Reference

The @code{<pipeline>} element is the root container of a Flow workflow
document. Attribute names are case-insensitive and accept @code{snake_case},
@code{kebab-case}, and dot (@code{.}) separators. String values support
@code{@{@{VariableName@}@}} interpolation.

@menu
* Databases and Pools::         @code{<databases>} and @code{<database>}.
* Variables Section::           @code{<variables>} and @code{<variable>}.
* Preflight and Flow::          @code{<preflight>} and @code{<flow>}.
* Control Flow Elements::       @code{<foreach>}, @code{<group>}, @code{<while>}, @code{<if>}, @code{<parallel>}.
* Task Elements::               Templates, SQL, KV, Assertions, File/Excel I/O, Path queries, HTTP.
@end menu

@node Databases and Pools
@section @code{<databases>} and @code{<database>}

@code{<databases>} is an optional container of @code{<database>} connection
definitions:

@table @code
@item name
(Mandatory) Unique handle referenced by @code{db}, @code{database}, or
@code{target_db}.
@item driver / type
Relational SQL (@code{sqlserver} [default], @code{postgres}, @code{mysql},
@code{sqlite}, @code{oracle}) or Key-Value (@code{bbolt}/@code{bolt},
@code{badger}, @code{redis}/@code{valkey}, @code{etcd}).
@item connection_string
(Mandatory) Driver DSN, URL, or path (supports @code{@{@{VariableName@}@}}).
@item workload
Pool tuning profile:
@itemize @bullet
@item @code{oltp} (default): @code{max_open_conns=25}, @code{max_idle_conns=10}, @code{conn_max_lifetime=5m}, @code{conn_max_idle_time=2m}.
@item @code{bulk}: @code{50} / @code{25} / @code{30m} / @code{10m}.
@item @code{analytics}: @code{15} / @code{8} / @code{30m} / @code{10m}.
@item @code{batch}: @code{20} / @code{10} / @code{15m} / @code{5m}.
@end itemize
@item max_open_conns, max_idle_conns
Explicit pool size overrides (@code{max_idle_conns} is clamped to @code{max_open_conns}).
@item conn_max_lifetime_seconds / conn_max_lifetime
Connection reuse lifetime (duration string like @code{5m} or integer seconds).
@item conn_max_idle_time_seconds / conn_max_idle_time
Idle connection timeout before closing (duration string like @code{2m} or integer seconds).
@item id, description
Optional identifier and human-readable description.
@end table

@node Variables Section
@section @code{<variables>} and @code{<variable>}

@code{<variables>} declares initial typed variables via @code{<variable>}:

@table @code
@item name
(Mandatory) Variable identifier for @code{@{@{VariableName@}@}} interpolation.
@item value
(Mandatory) Initial value parsed according to @code{type}.
@item type
@code{string} (default), @code{int}/@code{integer}, @code{bool}/@code{boolean},
@code{float}/@code{double}/@code{float64}, @code{datetime}, or @code{date}.
@item id, description
Optional metadata attributes.
@end table

@node Preflight and Flow
@section @code{<preflight>} and @code{<flow>}

@itemize @bullet
@item
@code{<preflight>}: Optional setup, smoke-test, and connectivity validation
container appearing once before @code{<flow>}. Executed standalone via
@command{flow -preflight}.
@item
@code{<flow>}: Main execution container. Child steps run sequentially in
document order unless wrapped in @code{<parallel>}, @code{<foreach>}, or
@code{<while>}.
@end itemize

@node Control Flow Elements
@section Control Flow and Logical Grouping

@subsection @code{<foreach>}
Runs nested child steps once per row returned by a SQL driver query on
@code{db} / @code{database} (inline SQL or @code{var} / @code{variable}).
Exposes columns in original, lowercase, and uppercase names, and sets
@code{LOOP_INDEX} (zero-based) on each iteration.

@subsection @code{<group>}
Sequential block supporting:
@itemize @bullet
@item Conditional execution: @code{var}/@code{if_var}, @code{equals}/@code{val}/@code{value}/@code{if_val}/@code{if_equals}, @code{condition}/@code{cond}.
@item Database transactions: @code{transaction="true"} (alias @code{tx}) on @code{db}/@code{database} commits on success and rolls back on failure.
@item Pinned database sessions: @code{session="true"} (aliases @code{pin_connection}, @code{pin_conn}, @code{sticky}) pins a single @code{*sql.Conn} so session-scoped temporary tables (@code{#Temp}, @code{CREATE TEMP TABLE}) persist across child steps and nested transactional groups.
@item Context deadline: @code{timeout} (e.g., @code{30s}, @code{5m}).
@end itemize

@subsection @code{<while>}
Repeats nested child steps while its condition (@code{var}/@code{if_var} and
@code{equals}/@code{if_equals}, or @code{condition}/@code{cond}) holds, up to
@code{max_iterations} / @code{max_loops} (default @code{1000}). Sets
@code{WHILE_INDEX} on each iteration.

@subsection @code{<if>}, @code{<then>}, @code{<else>}
Evaluates @code{var}/@code{if_var} + @code{equals}/@code{if_equals} or
@code{condition}/@code{cond}; runs @code{<then>} (or direct inline child
nodes) when true and @code{<else>} when false.

@subsection @code{<parallel>}
Runs nested child nodes concurrently across a goroutine pool controlled by
@code{max_threads} / @code{threads} / @code{concurrency} (default @code{0} =
unbounded). Thread-isolated variable snapshots merge safely on completion with
collision namespacing (@code{WORKER_<id>_<key>}).

@node Task Elements
@section Pipeline Task Elements

Most data-producing steps write to @code{LAST_OUTPUT} as well as any specified
output variable.

@table @code
@item <template> / <template_html>
Render Go @code{text/template} or XSS-safe @code{html/template} from
@code{file} or inline body. Attributes: @code{id} (mandatory), @code{name},
@code{file}, @code{engine}, @code{output_var}/@code{var}, @code{mode}
(@code{summary} or rendered text).

@item <sql>
Execute SQL on @code{db}/@code{database} from @code{var}/@code{variable} or
inline body; store result in @code{output_var}/@code{out_var}/@code{output_variable}.

@item <sql_bulk>
Stream rows from @code{db}/@code{database} into @code{target_table} on
@code{target_db}/@code{target_database} (defaults to source @code{db}).
Uses native TDS @code{CopyIn} for SQL Server (@code{tablock},
@code{check_constraints}, @code{fire_triggers}, @code{keep_nulls}) and
prepared multi-row batched @code{INSERT} statements for PostgreSQL, MySQL,
Oracle, and SQLite. Optional @code{batch_size} and @code{output_var}/@code{out_var}.

@item <kv>
Atomic Key-Value operations (@code{get}, @code{put}/@code{set},
@code{delete}/@code{del}, @code{scan}/@code{list}) against @code{db} in
@code{bucket} (default @code{default}) via attributes (@code{op}, @code{key},
@code{value}) or inline DSL text.

@item <kv_bulk>
Stream SQL query rows (col 1 = key, col 2 = value) from @code{db} into KV
@code{target_db} and @code{target_bucket}/@code{bucket} in batches
(@code{batch_size} default @code{10000}).

@item <assert>
Check @code{var} against @code{equals}/@code{value}. On failure, optionally
set @code{fail_var} to @code{fail_val} (default @code{true}), run nested
@code{<on_failure>} steps, and apply @code{on_failure} (@code{halt} [default],
@code{warn}, or @code{continue}).

@item <file_read> / <file_save>
Read @code{file}/@code{path}/@code{filename} into @code{var}/@code{output_var},
or write @code{var}/inline body to disk (@code{append="true"} appends; parent
directories are created automatically).

@item <excel_write> / <excel_read>
Create/update @code{file} (@file{.xlsx}, @code{sheet} default @code{Sheet1})
from SQL on @code{db}, or read a worksheet (@code{header="true"} default) as
a JSON array into @code{output_var}/@code{var}.

@item <json_path> / <yaml_path> / <xml_xpath>
Extract data from @code{file} or @code{var} into @code{output_var}/@code{out_var}:
@itemize @bullet
@item @code{<json_path>}: @code{path}/@code{jsonpath}; @code{mode} = @code{value} (default), @code{json}, @code{json_array}.
@item @code{<yaml_path>}: @code{path}/@code{yamlpath}; @code{mode} = @code{value} (default), @code{json}, @code{json_array}, @code{yaml}.
@item @code{<xml_xpath>}: @code{xpath}; @code{mode} = @code{text} (default), @code{xml}, @code{json_array}.
@end itemize

@item <http_client>
Execute HTTP requests against @code{uri}/@code{url} (@code{method} default
@code{GET}, @code{data}/inline body, @code{headers}, @code{content_type}).
Stores body in @code{var}/@code{output_var} and status code in
@code{status_code_var}/@code{status_var}. Supports @code{timeout},
@code{follow_redirects}, @code{max_redirects}, @code{cookie_jar}, @code{proxy},
TLS options (@code{tls_insecure_skip_verify}, @code{tls_handshake_timeout},
@code{tls_server_name}, @code{tls_min_version}, @code{tls_max_version}), and
transport pool tuning (@code{max_idle_conns}, @code{max_idle_conns_per_host}
[default @code{10}], @code{max_conns_per_host}, @code{idle_conn_timeout},
@code{response_header_timeout}, @code{expect_continue_timeout},
@code{max_response_header_bytes}, @code{write_buffer_size},
@code{read_buffer_size}, @code{force_attempt_http2}).
@end table

@bye
